{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When building a multi-stage form that has many stages, like so:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"image","src":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TanStack/form/main/docs/assets/stepper.png","alt":"Form stepper"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It's common for each step to have its own form. However, this complicates the form submission and validation process by requiring you to add complex logic."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Luckily, TanStack Form provides a way to build out sub-forms that make this kind of development trivial to implement: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.group(...)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To use a form group in TanStack Form, you'll create a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackFormController"},{"type":"text","value":", then use its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group"},{"type":"text","value":" directive like you would use its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field"},{"type":"text","value":" directive:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { LitElement, html } from 'lit'\nimport { customElement } from 'lit/decorators.js'\nimport { TanStackFormController } from '@tanstack/lit-form'\n\n@customElement('my-form')\nexport class MyForm extends LitElement {\n  #form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n    defaultValues: {\n      step1: {\n        name: '',\n      },\n      step2: {\n        age: 0,\n      },\n    },\n  })\n\n  render() {\n    return html`\n      ${this.#form.group({ name: 'step1' }, (group) => {\n        // `group` here has all of the form-like methods you'd expect like `deleteField` or `insertFieldValue`\n        // ...\n        return html``\n      })}\n    `\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This becomes much more useful when paired with external state to conditionally render a form group:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { LitElement, html, nothing } from 'lit'\nimport { customElement, state } from 'lit/decorators.js'\nimport { TanStackFormController } from '@tanstack/lit-form'\n\n@customElement('my-form')\nexport class MyForm extends LitElement {\n  @state()\n  private step = 0\n\n  #form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n    defaultValues: {\n      step1: {\n        name: '',\n      },\n      step2: {\n        age: 0,\n      },\n    },\n  })\n\n  render() {\n    return html`\n      ${this.step === 0\n        ? this.#form.group(\n            {\n              name: 'step1',\n              onGroupSubmit: () => {\n                // We can move the step forward when validation passes\n                this.step++\n              },\n              onGroupSubmitInvalid: () => {\n                // Or handle invalid submissions, just like a top-level form\n              },\n              onSubmitMeta: {} as SomeType,\n            },\n            (group) => html`\n              <form\n                @submit=${(e: Event) => {\n                  e.preventDefault()\n                  e.stopPropagation()\n                  // Use `group.handleSubmit()` to submit the sub-form, but not the parent form\n                  group.handleSubmit()\n                }}\n              >\n                ${this.#form.field(\n                  { name: 'step1.name' },\n                  (field) => html`<!-- ... -->`,\n                )}\n              </form>\n            `,\n          )\n        : nothing}\n      ${this.step === 1\n        ? this.#form.group(\n            {\n              name: 'step2',\n              onGroupSubmit: () => {\n                // Then, use `this.#form.api.handleSubmit()` to submit the entire form\n                this.#form.api.handleSubmit()\n              },\n            },\n            (group) => html`\n              <form\n                @submit=${(e: Event) => {\n                  e.preventDefault()\n                  e.stopPropagation()\n                  group.handleSubmit()\n                }}\n              >\n                ${this.#form.field(\n                  { name: 'step2.age' },\n                  (field) => html`<!-- ... -->`,\n                )}\n              </form>\n            `,\n          )\n        : nothing}\n    `\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When you split each step into its own custom element, pass the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackFormController"},{"type":"text","value":" as a property and type it with "},{"type":"link","href":"./form-composition.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFormType"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Because Lit child elements that receive a controller by property do not automatically re-render when the controller state changes, subscribe to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.api.store"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackStoreSelector"},{"type":"text","value":" in the child element."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"form-group-validation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Form Group Validation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Form groups have a distinct validation procedure that we think makes sense for sub-forms:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Form groups can have their own validation:"}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"${this.#form.group(\n  { name: 'step1', validators: { onChange: () => 'Error' } },\n  (group) => html`\n    <!-- group.state.meta.errorMap // {onChange: \"Error\" | undefined} -->\n    <!-- group.state.meta.errors // (\"Error\")[] -->\n  `,\n)}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Can set errors on sub-fields:"}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"${this.#form.group(\n  {\n    name: 'step1',\n    validators: {\n      onChange: ({ value, groupApi }) => ({\n        group: value.name === 'error' ? 'Group error' : undefined,\n        fields: {\n          // Must use the name of the field relative to the form group as the error key,\n          // to stay consistent with how standard schema works with form groups\n          name: value.name === 'error' ? 'Field error' : undefined,\n        },\n      }),\n    },\n  },\n  (group) => html`<!-- ... -->`,\n)}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"And can even accept standard schemas:"}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"${this.#form.group(\n  {\n    name: 'step1',\n    validators: {\n      onChange: z.object({\n        name: z.string().min(2),\n      }),\n    },\n  },\n  (group) => html`<!-- ... -->`,\n)}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The reason we don't use the full path names for fields is so that you can compose your schemas like so:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const step1Schema = z.object({\n  name: z.string().min(2),\n})\n\nconst schema = z.object({\n  step1: step1Schema,\n  step2: step2Schema,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"And pass the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"step1Schema"},{"type":"text","value":" to a form group and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"schema"},{"type":"text","value":" to the parent form. That way, partially validated data will still flag errors if the group is bypassed."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"dynamic-group-validation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dynamic Group Validation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you want to use "},{"type":"link","href":"./dynamic-validation.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"dynamic validation ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onDynamic"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with a form group, do not rely on the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onDynamic"},{"type":"text","value":" validator passed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackFormController"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"#form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n  validationLogic: revalidateLogic(),\n  validators: {\n    // This validator will not run `onChange` when a sub-form is submitted;\n    // it will only run `onChange` when the form itself is submitted.\n    onDynamic: schema,\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Instead, pass your sub-schema for the group to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onDynamic"},{"type":"text","value":" validation of the group itself:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"${this.#form.group(\n  { name: 'step1', validators: { onDynamic: step1Schema } },\n  (group) => html`<!-- ... -->`,\n)}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It will treat "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group.submissionAttempts"},{"type":"text","value":" as the way to change what validator is run before/after submit."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"form-group-state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Form Group State"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Just like you're able to access "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group.state.meta.errors"},{"type":"text","value":", you're also able to access the group's value using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group.state.value"},{"type":"text","value":". Likewise, here are some valuable properties you can access in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group.state.meta"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group.state.meta.isFieldsValid"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" when the field-level validators have no errors"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group.state.meta.isGroupValid"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" when the group-level validators have no errors"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group.state.meta.isValid"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" when both the field-level and group-level validators have no errors"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group.state.meta.isSubmitting"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" when the group is in the process of being submitted"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"usage","text":"Usage","level":2},{"id":"form-group-validation","text":"Form Group Validation","level":2},{"id":"dynamic-group-validation","text":"Dynamic Group Validation","level":3},{"id":"form-group-state","text":"Form Group State","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nWhen building a multi-stage form that has many stages, like so:\n\n![Form stepper](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TanStack/form/main/docs/assets/stepper.png)\n\nIt's common for each step to have its own form. However, this complicates the form submission and validation process by requiring you to add complex logic.\n\nLuckily, TanStack Form provides a way to build out sub-forms that make this kind of development trivial to implement: `form.group(...)`.\n\n## Usage\n\nTo use a form group in TanStack Form, you'll create a `TanStackFormController`, then use its `group` directive like you would use its `field` directive:\n\n```ts\nimport { LitElement, html } from 'lit'\nimport { customElement } from 'lit/decorators.js'\nimport { TanStackFormController } from '@tanstack/lit-form'\n\n@customElement('my-form')\nexport class MyForm extends LitElement {\n  #form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n    defaultValues: {\n      step1: {\n        name: '',\n      },\n      step2: {\n        age: 0,\n      },\n    },\n  })\n\n  render() {\n    return html`\n      ${this.#form.group({ name: 'step1' }, (group) => {\n        // `group` here has all of the form-like methods you'd expect like `deleteField` or `insertFieldValue`\n        // ...\n        return html``\n      })}\n    `\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis becomes much more useful when paired with external state to conditionally render a form group:\n\n```ts\nimport { LitElement, html, nothing } from 'lit'\nimport { customElement, state } from 'lit/decorators.js'\nimport { TanStackFormController } from '@tanstack/lit-form'\n\n@customElement('my-form')\nexport class MyForm extends LitElement {\n  @state()\n  private step = 0\n\n  #form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n    defaultValues: {\n      step1: {\n        name: '',\n      },\n      step2: {\n        age: 0,\n      },\n    },\n  })\n\n  render() {\n    return html`\n      ${this.step === 0\n        ? this.#form.group(\n            {\n              name: 'step1',\n              onGroupSubmit: () => {\n                // We can move the step forward when validation passes\n                this.step++\n              },\n              onGroupSubmitInvalid: () => {\n                // Or handle invalid submissions, just like a top-level form\n              },\n              onSubmitMeta: {} as SomeType,\n            },\n            (group) => html`\n              <form\n                @submit=${(e: Event) => {\n                  e.preventDefault()\n                  e.stopPropagation()\n                  // Use `group.handleSubmit()` to submit the sub-form, but not the parent form\n                  group.handleSubmit()\n                }}\n              >\n                ${this.#form.field(\n                  { name: 'step1.name' },\n                  (field) => html`<!-- ... -->`,\n                )}\n              </form>\n            `,\n          )\n        : nothing}\n      ${this.step === 1\n        ? this.#form.group(\n            {\n              name: 'step2',\n              onGroupSubmit: () => {\n                // Then, use `this.#form.api.handleSubmit()` to submit the entire form\n                this.#form.api.handleSubmit()\n              },\n            },\n            (group) => html`\n              <form\n                @submit=${(e: Event) => {\n                  e.preventDefault()\n                  e.stopPropagation()\n                  group.handleSubmit()\n                }}\n              >\n                ${this.#form.field(\n                  { name: 'step2.age' },\n                  (field) => html`<!-- ... -->`,\n                )}\n              </form>\n            `,\n          )\n        : nothing}\n    `\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWhen you split each step into its own custom element, pass the `TanStackFormController` as a property and type it with [`getFormType`](./form-composition.md). Because Lit child elements that receive a controller by property do not automatically re-render when the controller state changes, subscribe to `form.api.store` with `TanStackStoreSelector` in the child element.\n\n## Form Group Validation\n\nForm groups have a distinct validation procedure that we think makes sense for sub-forms:\n\n- Form groups can have their own validation:\n\n```ts\n${this.#form.group(\n  { name: 'step1', validators: { onChange: () => 'Error' } },\n  (group) => html`\n    <!-- group.state.meta.errorMap // {onChange: \"Error\" | undefined} -->\n    <!-- group.state.meta.errors // (\"Error\")[] -->\n  `,\n)}\n```\n\n- Can set errors on sub-fields:\n\n```ts\n${this.#form.group(\n  {\n    name: 'step1',\n    validators: {\n      onChange: ({ value, groupApi }) => ({\n        group: value.name === 'error' ? 'Group error' : undefined,\n        fields: {\n          // Must use the name of the field relative to the form group as the error key,\n          // to stay consistent with how standard schema works with form groups\n          name: value.name === 'error' ? 'Field error' : undefined,\n        },\n      }),\n    },\n  },\n  (group) => html`<!-- ... -->`,\n)}\n```\n\n- And can even accept standard schemas:\n\n```ts\n${this.#form.group(\n  {\n    name: 'step1',\n    validators: {\n      onChange: z.object({\n        name: z.string().min(2),\n      }),\n    },\n  },\n  (group) => html`<!-- ... -->`,\n)}\n```\n\n> The reason we don't use the full path names for fields is so that you can compose your schemas like so:\n>\n> ```ts\n> const step1Schema = z.object({\n>   name: z.string().min(2),\n> })\n>\n> const schema = z.object({\n>   step1: step1Schema,\n>   step2: step2Schema,\n> })\n> ```\n>\n> And pass the `step1Schema` to a form group and `schema` to the parent form. That way, partially validated data will still flag errors if the group is bypassed.\n\n### Dynamic Group Validation\n\nIf you want to use [dynamic validation (`onDynamic`)](./dynamic-validation.md) with a form group, do not rely on the `onDynamic` validator passed to `TanStackFormController`:\n\n```ts\n#form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n  validationLogic: revalidateLogic(),\n  validators: {\n    // This validator will not run `onChange` when a sub-form is submitted;\n    // it will only run `onChange` when the form itself is submitted.\n    onDynamic: schema,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nInstead, pass your sub-schema for the group to the `onDynamic` validation of the group itself:\n\n```ts\n${this.#form.group(\n  { name: 'step1', validators: { onDynamic: step1Schema } },\n  (group) => html`<!-- ... -->`,\n)}\n```\n\nIt will treat `group.submissionAttempts` as the way to change what validator is run before/after submit.\n\n## Form Group State\n\nJust like you're able to access `group.state.meta.errors`, you're also able to access the group's value using `group.state.value`. Likewise, here are some valuable properties you can access in the `group.state.meta`:\n\n- `group.state.meta.isFieldsValid`: `true` when the field-level validators have no errors\n- `group.state.meta.isGroupValid`: `true` when the group-level validators have no errors\n- `group.state.meta.isValid`: `true` when both the field-level and group-level validators have no errors\n- `group.state.meta.isSubmitting`: `true` when the group is in the process of being submitted\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: form-groups\ntitle: Form Groups\n---\n\nWhen building a multi-stage form that has many stages, like so:\n\n![Form stepper](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TanStack/form/main/docs/assets/stepper.png)\n\nIt's common for each step to have its own form. However, this complicates the form submission and validation process by requiring you to add complex logic.\n\nLuckily, TanStack Form provides a way to build out sub-forms that make this kind of development trivial to implement: `form.group(...)`.\n\n## Usage\n\nTo use a form group in TanStack Form, you'll create a `TanStackFormController`, then use its `group` directive like you would use its `field` directive:\n\n```ts\nimport { LitElement, html } from 'lit'\nimport { customElement } from 'lit/decorators.js'\nimport { TanStackFormController } from '@tanstack/lit-form'\n\n@customElement('my-form')\nexport class MyForm extends LitElement {\n  #form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n    defaultValues: {\n      step1: {\n        name: '',\n      },\n      step2: {\n        age: 0,\n      },\n    },\n  })\n\n  render() {\n    return html`\n      ${this.#form.group({ name: 'step1' }, (group) => {\n        // `group` here has all of the form-like methods you'd expect like `deleteField` or `insertFieldValue`\n        // ...\n        return html``\n      })}\n    `\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis becomes much more useful when paired with external state to conditionally render a form group:\n\n```ts\nimport { LitElement, html, nothing } from 'lit'\nimport { customElement, state } from 'lit/decorators.js'\nimport { TanStackFormController } from '@tanstack/lit-form'\n\n@customElement('my-form')\nexport class MyForm extends LitElement {\n  @state()\n  private step = 0\n\n  #form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n    defaultValues: {\n      step1: {\n        name: '',\n      },\n      step2: {\n        age: 0,\n      },\n    },\n  })\n\n  render() {\n    return html`\n      ${this.step === 0\n        ? this.#form.group(\n            {\n              name: 'step1',\n              onGroupSubmit: () => {\n                // We can move the step forward when validation passes\n                this.step++\n              },\n              onGroupSubmitInvalid: () => {\n                // Or handle invalid submissions, just like a top-level form\n              },\n              onSubmitMeta: {} as SomeType,\n            },\n            (group) => html`\n              <form\n                @submit=${(e: Event) => {\n                  e.preventDefault()\n                  e.stopPropagation()\n                  // Use `group.handleSubmit()` to submit the sub-form, but not the parent form\n                  group.handleSubmit()\n                }}\n              >\n                ${this.#form.field(\n                  { name: 'step1.name' },\n                  (field) => html`<!-- ... -->`,\n                )}\n              </form>\n            `,\n          )\n        : nothing}\n      ${this.step === 1\n        ? this.#form.group(\n            {\n              name: 'step2',\n              onGroupSubmit: () => {\n                // Then, use `this.#form.api.handleSubmit()` to submit the entire form\n                this.#form.api.handleSubmit()\n              },\n            },\n            (group) => html`\n              <form\n                @submit=${(e: Event) => {\n                  e.preventDefault()\n                  e.stopPropagation()\n                  group.handleSubmit()\n                }}\n              >\n                ${this.#form.field(\n                  { name: 'step2.age' },\n                  (field) => html`<!-- ... -->`,\n                )}\n              </form>\n            `,\n          )\n        : nothing}\n    `\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWhen you split each step into its own custom element, pass the `TanStackFormController` as a property and type it with [`getFormType`](./form-composition.md). Because Lit child elements that receive a controller by property do not automatically re-render when the controller state changes, subscribe to `form.api.store` with `TanStackStoreSelector` in the child element.\n\n## Form Group Validation\n\nForm groups have a distinct validation procedure that we think makes sense for sub-forms:\n\n- Form groups can have their own validation:\n\n```ts\n${this.#form.group(\n  { name: 'step1', validators: { onChange: () => 'Error' } },\n  (group) => html`\n    <!-- group.state.meta.errorMap // {onChange: \"Error\" | undefined} -->\n    <!-- group.state.meta.errors // (\"Error\")[] -->\n  `,\n)}\n```\n\n- Can set errors on sub-fields:\n\n```ts\n${this.#form.group(\n  {\n    name: 'step1',\n    validators: {\n      onChange: ({ value, groupApi }) => ({\n        group: value.name === 'error' ? 'Group error' : undefined,\n        fields: {\n          // Must use the name of the field relative to the form group as the error key,\n          // to stay consistent with how standard schema works with form groups\n          name: value.name === 'error' ? 'Field error' : undefined,\n        },\n      }),\n    },\n  },\n  (group) => html`<!-- ... -->`,\n)}\n```\n\n- And can even accept standard schemas:\n\n```ts\n${this.#form.group(\n  {\n    name: 'step1',\n    validators: {\n      onChange: z.object({\n        name: z.string().min(2),\n      }),\n    },\n  },\n  (group) => html`<!-- ... -->`,\n)}\n```\n\n> The reason we don't use the full path names for fields is so that you can compose your schemas like so:\n>\n> ```ts\n> const step1Schema = z.object({\n>   name: z.string().min(2),\n> })\n>\n> const schema = z.object({\n>   step1: step1Schema,\n>   step2: step2Schema,\n> })\n> ```\n>\n> And pass the `step1Schema` to a form group and `schema` to the parent form. That way, partially validated data will still flag errors if the group is bypassed.\n\n### Dynamic Group Validation\n\nIf you want to use [dynamic validation (`onDynamic`)](./dynamic-validation.md) with a form group, do not rely on the `onDynamic` validator passed to `TanStackFormController`:\n\n```ts\n#form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n  validationLogic: revalidateLogic(),\n  validators: {\n    // This validator will not run `onChange` when a sub-form is submitted;\n    // it will only run `onChange` when the form itself is submitted.\n    onDynamic: schema,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nInstead, pass your sub-schema for the group to the `onDynamic` validation of the group itself:\n\n```ts\n${this.#form.group(\n  { name: 'step1', validators: { onDynamic: step1Schema } },\n  (group) => html`<!-- ... -->`,\n)}\n```\n\nIt will treat `group.submissionAttempts` as the way to change what validator is run before/after submit.\n\n## Form Group State\n\nJust like you're able to access `group.state.meta.errors`, you're also able to access the group's value using `group.state.value`. Likewise, here are some valuable properties you can access in the `group.state.meta`:\n\n- `group.state.meta.isFieldsValid`: `true` when the field-level validators have no errors\n- `group.state.meta.isGroupValid`: `true` when the group-level validators have no errors\n- `group.state.meta.isValid`: `true` when both the field-level and group-level validators have no errors\n- `group.state.meta.isSubmitting`: `true` when the group is in the process of being submitted\n"}
